  "question_type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ be such that $|\\vec{a}| = |\\vec{b}| = a$, and the angle between them is $\\theta$. For which value(s) of $\\theta$ is $|\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}| = |\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}|$?",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "$|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}|^2 = |\\vec{a}|^2 + |\\vec{b}|^2 + 2|\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\cos\\theta = 2a^2 + 2a^2\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />$|\\vec{a}-\\vec{b}|^2 = 2a^2 - 2a^2\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />Set equal:<br /><br />$2a^2 + 2a^2\\cos\\theta = 2a^2 - 2a^2\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />$\\implies 4a^2\\cos\\theta = 0$<br /><br />$\\implies \\cos\\theta = 0$<br /><br />$\\implies \\theta = 90^\\circ$",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\theta = 0$",
    "B": "$\\theta = 90^\\circ$",
    "C": "$\\theta = 120^\\circ$",
    "D": "$\\theta = 180^\\circ$"
  },
